# Click the thing he sees (HARD)

**Owner 2026-09-01.** Agents spent ~10 turns centering hero stars and review cards. The broken surface was the Home Instagram / Juicer feed (`@barreletics`). Computed math on the wrong wrapper is not a fix.

## Target = the pixels he sent

If Andrew pastes a screenshot or quotes on-page copy, the target is **that heading + that media**.

Match the visible words. Then open that section. Then measure that wrapper.

```
✅ Screenshot shows “@barreletics” / “Real practitioners. Real studios. Real grip.”
   → home-juicer.liquid · .j-stacker-wrapper / .feed-item
❌ “He said Judge.me, so it must be hero stars or pdp-reviews”
```

## Forbidden remaps

| He shows / says | Is NOT |
|---|---|
| Judge.me / review cards | Hero `.split-hero__trust` / “Trusted by…” |
| Hero stars / Trusted by | Instagram feed |
| `@barreletics` / juicer photos | Mosaic, reviews, 50/50 |
| Mosaic tiles (“Secure in every hold”) | Juicer or reviews |

If the exact heading is not on the page → **STOP. Ask. Do not pick a neighbor.**

## Before writing CSS

1. Name: section file · wrapper selector · visible heading
2. Screenshot **that** block at the viewport he named
3. Pass = left/right margins of **his visible tiles**, not a parent that happens to be centered
4. One surface. No hero / mosaic / One Pair / Coperni / JSON unless he named them

## Do not claim verified

- From DOM math on a different section
- From “there is no Judge.me widget, so it must be X”
- From Theme Editor with the sidebar open
